   "The sheet prints the process as CR-56 only (the E-6 compatible Fuji process) and the densitometry as 'Fuji FAD-30S (Status A equivalent)'. Exposure: daylight. x axis of curves is log H in lux-seconds as printed. RMS granularity 7: diffuse, 48 um aperture, sample density 1.0 (page 7).",
   "curves: r solid, g dash-dot, b dashed. On the plateau r 3.31, b 3.45, g 3.50 (the g plateau lies exactly on the 3.5 grid line). b runs on r from log H -2.3 to about -2.05; g stays 0.04 above them until log H -2.1. All three meet in one ink blob near log H -2.0 (D 2.9) and r then runs above the g/b band (by about 0.07-0.09 until log H -1.5), as in Velvia 50; g and b are about 0.04 apart at log H -1.84..-1.80 and share one dashed band otherwise. Below log H -1.45 all three coincide within about 0.03 and are traced alike. Curves end at log H 1.0 (D-min plateau 0.13).",
   "sensitivity: y is relative log sensitivity as printed (sensitivity = reciprocal of the exposure in J/cm2 giving minimum density + 1.0). Curves are drawn from about -0.7 up to the peak and down again: b 395-521 nm, g 479-600 nm, r 549-683 nm; the end drops are near vertical, so the last 1-3 nm are only approximated on the 5 nm grid.",
   "dyes: spectral diffuse density of the separated dyes (max 1.0) as printed; curves start at about 394 nm (yellow 396) and cyan ends at about 711 nm (D 0.29). Yellow is not traced beyond 555 nm and magenta beyond 660 nm where they join the base line (about 0.01). The upper-left curve at 394 nm is cyan, the lower one magenta; they cross near 437 nm (both about 0.035). Yellow/magenta cross near 496 nm, yellow/cyan near 525 nm, magenta/cyan near 590 nm (D 0.43)."
